# Download-on-launch: a 0-byte stub means the ROM isn't on the card -> the wrap brings the
# engine in (--download, now via run_with_progress for a REAL engine-driven bar + retry-resume,
# T1.3), the stub fills in place, and the stock launcher runs the real file. The progress panel
# is engine-driven (its appearance races the instant stub), so we assert the STABLE observables:
# the --download call, the filled file, and the stock hand-off (parity with m-menu-sync-now).
desc fetch: 0-byte stub -> --download fills it, stock launcher runs
invoke wrap
config paired
wifi up
sdfile Roms/GBA/Zelda.gba
engine 0|RESULT downloaded=1
engine 0|LOCAL=none
engine 0|RESULT mode=list-states n=0
expect_exit 0
expect_trace ENGINE --download
expect_file_has Roms/GBA/Zelda.gba DLBYTES
expect_trace STOCK GBA rom=
